[N 37-39 Riverglades]
[D Forever Shaman 30-60 (Braedyn)\\The Riverglades, new to Forever: Southern Watch and the Bristle Hills gnolls, Turner's Logging Camp, Farholde Keep (flight point, inn, the chapel and the training grounds), Wheeler's Grange, Terral's Watch and Sunnyglade with the caves beneath it. Then the level-40 block begins with chapter 39 (Arathi via Stormwind).]
[GA Alliance]
[OC]|cffffffffLevel 37|r  -  this chapter wants level 37: every quest needs only 36, but the Bristle Hills gnolls are 36-38, the Mudfin Warriors 37-38, the Rog'mar poachers and the lions 38-39 and the Sunnyglade cultists and the cave beneath it 37-41 (Raiders 40, Ritualists 39-41). Under 37: Southern Watch, Farholde Keep, Wheeler's Grange and Terral's Watch come first anyway and Sunnyglade is the last leg, so you meet it at your highest level
[OC]|cffffffffThe Riverglades|r  -  new to Forever, east of Redridge; the Alliance hub is Farholde Keep in the south-east. About 63,700 quest XP from 32 hand-ins and every kill target is a normal mob (the elites are named below: keep clear). You arrive from Booty Bay with hearth = Thelsamar and bind at Farholde Keep. Rog'mar in the middle of the zone (57-60,43-47) is a Horde town with level-55 guards: every leg goes round it
[OC]|cffffcc00Sources:|r givers, hand-ins and NPC positions come from the DB; most quest objects have no position in it, and those points come from Wowhead's maps. The order of the chains below follows the prerequisites QuestieDB 1.1.1 takes from player traces: Benjy Wheeler, Sister Rowland, Bertrand Ironbrow and Watcher Cornelius each hand out their next quest only when the one before is handed in
[OC]|cffffcc00Carried in:|r Deliver the Second Shipment (94929, from Watcher Biggs in chapter 37) is handed in at Demar Brant in Farholde Keep. Shaman: Storm, Earth, and Fire (79358, all four totems) rides on to Veyric in chapter 39
[OC]|cffffcc00Training:|r no shaman trainer in the Riverglades; the next ranks wait for Ironforge in chapter 39d

[OC]|cffffffffInto the Riverglades|r  -  Lakeshire is the nearest flight path you know; Farholde Keep's is not known yet, so the first trip is by road. The road east out of Redridge is not in the data: the points below are Lakeshire's flight master and Southern Watch, the first Alliance post; the way between them is unverified
At [TAR2859 Gyll], |cFFfff8a3Fly to [F Lakeshire]|r (the game routes it through Darkshire) [G27.5,77.8 Stranglethorn Vale]
